  "knownDifferences": [
    "GeoMoose 3.15.2 does not add OpenGeo bearer or organization headers. The exact client module can exchange the WFS body and GML2 representation, but direct access to a private OpenGeo endpoint still requires the authenticated OpenGeo host or a separately governed public publication.",
    "The exact OpenLayers writer emits EPSG:4326 spatial-filter coordinates as longitude/latitude while its GML2 reader honors the WFS 1.1 authority axis and reads latitude/longitude output. OpenGeo bounds this asymmetric client behavior explicitly; the reader also materializes a zero Z coordinate.",
    "OpenGeo retains WFS 2.0/GML 3.2 as canonical. WFS 1.1 compatibility is limited to GetFeature with the declared KVP/XML, CRS, filter, size, and output bounds; WFS 1.1 capabilities, schema discovery, stored queries, and transactions are not claimed by this fixture.",
